{"title":"2013 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer. For any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> and positive real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, define \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/59838efe579d7932f02643d88449c449d93f7d59.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f_j(r) =\\min (jr, n)+\\min\\left(\\frac{j}{r}, n\\right),\\text{ and }g_j(r) =\\min (\\lceil jr\\rceil, n)+\\min\\left(\\left\\lceil\\frac{j}{r}\\right\\rceil, n\\right),\\]\" width=\"592\" height=\"43\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/82590973296fc625b88ad4b4d9c762f3ef07b9b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lceil x\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> denotes the smallest integer greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/69378627bf482631c8a7157b50157ae7a86d3b97.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j=1}^n f_j(r)\\leq n^2+n\\leq \\sum_{j=1}^n g_j(r)\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"49\" />\nfor all positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First thing to note on both functions is the following:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e8516d484abda1df57dd6888a6102373ad172a16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_j\\left(\\frac{1}{r}\\right) =\\min\\left(\\frac{j}{r}, n\\right)+\\min (jr, n)=f_j(r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"340\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c5343a33a134d0f86cd15b1e7a3ae31b60301f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_j \\left( \\frac{1}{r} \\right) =\\min\\left(\\left\\lceil\\frac{j}{r}\\right\\rceil, n\\right)+\\min (\\lceil jr\\rceil, n)=g_j(r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"381\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Thus, we are going to look at two cases:\\.  When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/1930619a38fceee8e02990ea79026a348193307e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, and when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/9066f25538d897b813554873248c9b81a6646de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> which is the same as when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/804f706e4f51e30c6a8bc1fd4100cfa7d6abf5cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;r&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Case 1:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/1930619a38fceee8e02990ea79026a348193307e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50f3a9774e8d21b63aca9308aa8eac690e210e3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> in the sum, then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4e593dbfefb65cac914c2fd57408d5f99514c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_j(1) =\\min (j, n)+\\min (j, n)=2j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"271\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ecc6513dc0b3d31a75a28d6e150f905a2efc507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n f_j(1)=2\\sum_{j=1}^n j =n^2+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"219\" height=\"55\" />, and the equality holds.\n</p><p>Likewise,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/5/b15328539542d73817994d191a172d844624b72e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_j(1) =\\min (\\lceil j\\rceil, n)+\\min (\\lceil j\\rceil, n)=2\\lceil j\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"321\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> is integer we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/5/3656a0cefc6ef6ab1b807e0b80c2c36cbd875714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n g_j(1)=2\\sum_{j=1}^n \\lceil j\\rceil =2\\sum_{j=1}^n j = n^2+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"305\" height=\"55\" />, and the equality holds.\n</p><p>Thus for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/1930619a38fceee8e02990ea79026a348193307e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> we have equality as:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/9/049119a8597997a2b7c15184919c4fc3b8beb0c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n f_j(1) = n^2+n = \\sum_{j=1}^n g_j(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"237\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Case:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/9066f25538d897b813554873248c9b81a6646de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50f3a9774e8d21b63aca9308aa8eac690e210e3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ec2d3755a79fd9f7c4e8331a88d8b5ce720fe23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min\\left(\\frac{j}{r}, n\\right)=\\frac{j}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"130\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/8/588322c76a837e56c696e3d24f62e4d396a3479e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_j(r)=\\begin{cases} n+\\frac{j}{r}\\; , &amp; j &gt; \\frac{n}{r} \\\\                        jr+\\frac{j}{r}\\; , &amp; j \\le \\frac{n}{r}\\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"203\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/0/4f0eb85166dbada3f520b0bbd932719a1ab1ee82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n f_j(r)=r\\sum_{j=1}^{\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{r} \\right\\rfloor}j+\\sum_{j=\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{r} \\right\\rfloor +1}^{n}n+\\frac{1}{r}\\sum_{j=1}^{n}j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -33px\" width=\"317\" height=\"75\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/b/09be9d2e37fd74986672edea2f442b8023b8e612.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n f_j(r)=\\frac{r \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{r} \\right\\rfloor \\left( \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{r} \\right\\rfloor+1 \\right)}{2}+\\left( n-\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{r} \\right\\rfloor \\right)r +\\frac{n^2+n}{2r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"417\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a081739dc53fe935be08253d5b8f2b903bd4e6f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{r} \\right\\rfloor \\le \\frac{n}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"35\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/9/569e9a911aba24209cd22fa029a1b227961c8846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n f_j(r)&lt;\\frac{r}{2}\\left( \\frac{n}{r} \\right)\\left( \\frac{n}{r}+1 \\right)+n\\left( n- \\frac{n}{r}\\right)+\\frac{n^2+n}{2r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"399\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aefbb750f78720ea0cc4372860f333e2b4b9265.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n f_j(r) &lt; n^2 \\left( \\frac{1}{2r}+1-\\frac{1}{r}+ \\frac{1}{2r}\\right)+\\left( \\frac{1}{2} +\\frac{1}{2r}\\right)n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"393\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/0/de054c883dad2e3ff5fa978928809ef48a39b34a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n f_j(r) &lt; n^2 +\\left( \\frac{1}{2} +\\frac{1}{2r}\\right)n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"231\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/9066f25538d897b813554873248c9b81a6646de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a653267824f740ebfd5d861b7853cf9bddb1bc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2r} &lt; \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502602150bfd6f5a5059ec73c9c59d063b9ec0cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2r}+\\frac{1}{2} &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"92\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/b/41b87198129c1835ce786fbd8548fe2688165681.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( \\frac{1}{2r}+\\frac{1}{2} \\right)n &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"134\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdcdbc274a0fe997c813a77a2d104d8a1aec5e9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2+\\left( \\frac{1}{2r}+\\frac{1}{2} \\right)n &lt; n^2+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"215\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c22925d9c97e76c8f6c70715760eb1d6bf93089.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n f_j(r) &lt; n^2+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"145\" height=\"55\" />, which together with the equality case of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/1930619a38fceee8e02990ea79026a348193307e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> proves the left side of the equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/2466a1cd8840d21beb08fd24a625ccdf18bd2dcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n f_j(r) \\le n^2+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"145\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Now we look at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/0/6c0317bc4bad8d612f527335bb801ec85f0b4850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_j(r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50f3a9774e8d21b63aca9308aa8eac690e210e3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/2/c0288b1ae7589ae1ad6c3f678b33fdd0bb308983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min\\left(\\left\\lceil\\frac{j}{r}\\right\\rceil, n\\right)=\\left\\lceil\\frac{j}{r}\\right\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"174\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d68ba3a403d886323dd91e3006e0e07f0a22f02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_j(r)=\\begin{cases} n+\\left\\lceil \\frac{j}{r} \\right\\rceil\\; , &amp; \\left\\lceil jr \\right\\rceil &gt; n \\\\                        \\left\\lceil jr \\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil \\frac{j}{r} \\right\\rceil\\; , &amp; \\left\\lceil jr \\right\\rceil \\le n \\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"262\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/0/14035d7e836347ed62f3400bc579b654c06cb111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n g_j(r)=\\sum_{j=1}^{\\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{r} \\right\\rceil}\\left\\lceil jr \\right\\rceil+\\sum_{j=\\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{r} \\right\\rceil +1}^{n}n+\\sum_{j=1}^{n}\\left\\lceil \\frac{j}{r} \\right\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -33px\" width=\"338\" height=\"75\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/565081c5f0bb1674a048540a175bbf306667cd2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n g_j(r) \\ge \\sum_{j=1}^{\\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{r} \\right\\rceil} jr +\\sum_{j=\\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{r} \\right\\rceil +1}^{n}n+\\sum_{j=1}^{n}\\left\\lceil \\frac{j}{r} \\right\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -33px\" width=\"322\" height=\"75\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f67194c74ea729d99c2e42868337409494890295.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n g_j(r) &gt; \\frac{r}{2}\\left( \\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{r} \\right\\rceil \\right)\\left( \\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{r} \\right\\rceil+1 \\right)+n\\left( n- \\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{r} \\right\\rceil\\right)+\\sum_{j=1}^{n}\\left\\lceil \\frac{j}{r} \\right\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"462\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/f/6cfed4d230e041407fc302d94a78eddd0c07cde4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{r} \\right\\rceil \\ge \\frac{n}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"35\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/d/58d04dcbd23ff98da174aa16cb560eb63240fedc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n g_j(r) &gt; \\frac{r}{2}\\left( \\frac{n}{r} \\right)\\left( \\frac{n}{r}+1 \\right)+n\\left( n- \\frac{n}{r}\\right)+\\sum_{j=1}^{n}\\left\\lceil \\frac{j}{r} \\right\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"406\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a whole number and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> we notice the following:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c721ab2c3896781501f79d6f2361977f7a266c44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^{n}\\left\\lceil \\frac{j}{r} \\right\\rceil=\\frac{n(n+r)}{2r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"159\" height=\"55\" /> \n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> then we add more ceiling terms to the expression.  Likewise, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is not a whole number and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/9066f25538d897b813554873248c9b81a6646de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, the sum is larger.\n</p><p>Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/e/7eeafe8970bd4755df5c7d0be831a213429d3d4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^{n}\\left\\lceil \\frac{j}{r} \\right\\rceil \\ge \\frac{n(n+r)}{2r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"159\" height=\"55\" /> \n</p><p>Hence,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/354cf6376dc7558f318d6ff9a01050f87beb4b0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n g_j(r) &gt; \\frac{r}{2}\\left( \\frac{n}{r} \\right)\\left( \\frac{n}{r}+1 \\right)+n\\left( n- \\frac{n}{r}\\right)+\\frac{n(n+r)}{2r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"414\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/34971017fa07f9ac8b6c80cc9eaf1c445ae285b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n g_j(r) &gt; n^2 \\left( \\frac{1}{2r}+1-\\frac{1}{r}+ \\frac{1}{2r}\\right)+\\left( \\frac{1}{2} +\\frac{r}{2r}\\right)n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"393\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cba8ff3917e5a0562d6f7ebff9820ece2d9dc25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n g_j(r) &gt; n^2+\\left( \\frac{1}{2} +\\frac{1}{2}\\right)n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"222\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/1/2d163ebf2afd0ac5a8e3f809c7cfe7c66a58077b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n g_j(r) &gt; n^2+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"145\" height=\"55\" /> which together with the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/1930619a38fceee8e02990ea79026a348193307e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37efa5201ffe20078579180e595a622ef776173e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n g_j(r) \\ge n^2+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"145\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>and together with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2f2a8fbc4648f2501563d75bad1760209deaa62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_j(r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f89c2c1a257d99d9d703344a1ff179405d923fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^n f_j(r)\\leq n^2+n\\leq \\sum_{j=1}^n g_j(r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"233\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>~Tomas Diaz. orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232646\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 224/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 368/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14946/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.452      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    5.452      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25916:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017232646 and revision id 206171. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}